{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1785764357943,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":16,\"total_score\":5,\"scores\":{\"situation\":5,\"task\":0,\"action\":0,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate acknowledges a mistake, which is a positive first step.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response ‘idk’ provides absolutely no context. The interviewer needs to understand the situation, what the candidate was responsible for, and what they did or didn't do.\",\"This answer fails to demonstrate any self-awareness or reflection, which are crucial elements of learning from mistakes.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response is extremely weak and doesn’t provide any useful information. The interviewer needs a starting point – even a brief description of the situation would be beneficial. To improve, the candidate needs to attempt to articulate *something* about the project they were working on and the mistake they made. Even a single sentence attempting to describe the context would significantly increase the score.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"I understand you’re struggling to recall details at this moment. Let's try a different approach. Could you tell me about a time when you encountered an unexpected challenge on a project? It doesn’t need to be a major issue, just something that presented a difficulty.\"}"]}
