{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1785764383220,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":17,\"total_score\":0,\"scores\":{\"situation\":0,\"task\":0,\"action\":0,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"Honesty - The candidate immediately acknowledges they don't have an answer.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The candidate needs to demonstrate the ability to handle a common and important situation.  This response provides absolutely no insight into their skills or approach.\",\"A follow-up question should be asked to understand why the candidate doesn't have an example. Was it a difficult experience they don’t want to revisit? Did they not encounter such a situation?\"],\"feedback\":\"This is a completely insufficient response. The interviewer needs to hear a story, even a brief one, to assess how the candidate handles shifting priorities.  The candidate needs to provide *something* – any detail about a time they adapted, however small. This answer requires immediate clarification and redirection.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"I understand your question is asking for an example of adapting to changing requirements. Unfortunately, I don’t have one readily available at this moment. However, I can tell you that I recognize the importance of being flexible and responsive in a project environment.  Could you perhaps help me by describing the type of projects you're most interested in hearing about – for instance, are there specific types of changes or priorities you often see?\"}"]}
