{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1785764817779,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":23,\"total_score\":5,\"scores\":{\"situation\":5,\"task\":0,\"action\":0,\"result\":0},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate acknowledges they encountered a mistake, which is a positive first step.\"],\"improvements\":[\"The response ‘idk’ provides absolutely no context and fails to address the core of the question. It doesn't demonstrate self-awareness or an ability to reflect on a challenging situation.\",\"To provide a useful answer, the candidate needs to elaborate *at all* about the project they are referring to. Even a brief description would allow for a more detailed evaluation.\"],\"feedback\":\"This response is extremely weak and doesn't demonstrate any of the skills required to handle this type of interview question. The candidate needs to provide even a minimal amount of information about the situation, their role, and what happened. I recommend practicing using the STAR method (Situation, Task, Action, Result) to structure your responses to behavioral questions.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"I understand you're struggling to articulate this experience right now. Let’s work through it together. Can you tell me a little bit about a project you worked on recently? Just a few sentences describing the project would be a great start. Once we have that context, we can then explore what went wrong, your role in it, and what you learned.\"}"]}
