{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786110260823,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"session_id\":24,\"questions\":[{\"question_id\":100,\"question_order\":1,\"question\":\"Tell me about a time you faced a significant technical challenge while working on a project. How did you approach understanding the problem, and what was the outcome?\"},{\"question_id\":101,\"question_order\":2,\"question\":\"Describe a situation where you had to collaborate with someone who had a different perspective or opinion than your own. What steps did you take to ensure a productive resolution?\"},{\"question_id\":102,\"question_order\":3,\"question\":\"Share an example of a time when you made a mistake on a project – it doesn’t have to be a major failure. What did you learn from the experience, and how did you apply that learning moving forward?\"},{\"question_id\":103,\"question_order\":4,\"question\":\"Can you walk me through a situation where you had to adapt to changing requirements or priorities during a software development cycle? How did you manage your time and communicate those changes to your team?\"},{\"question_id\":104,\"question_order\":5,\"question\":\"Describe a time you took initiative to improve a process or solve a problem, even though it wasn’t explicitly part of your assigned tasks. What motivated you, and what was the result?\"}]}"]}
