{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786110555628,"level":"log","data":["Response body:","{\"answer_id\":35,\"total_score\":45,\"scores\":{\"situation\":15,\"task\":10,\"action\":12,\"result\":8},\"strengths\":[\"The candidate clearly identifies the core issue: changing code without thorough testing.\",\"They articulate a direct consequence of their action – another part of the application stopped working.\",\"The narrative flows logically from mistake to resolution.\"],\"improvements\":[\"**Situation (15/25):** The description is adequate, but could benefit from slightly more context. Adding one or two sentences about *why* they were changing the code would strengthen this. For example: 'While working on a software project focused on implementing user authentication...' This provides a better understanding of the situation.\",\"**Task (10/25):** The candidate states their responsibility – ‘changing some of the code’ – but doesn't explicitly state *what* they were trying to achieve with that change. Adding a brief explanation of the goal would improve clarity. For example: '…I was changing the code to update the user login functionality.'\"],\"feedback\":\"This is a solid, honest response demonstrating self-awareness and learning. The candidate clearly explains what happened and the immediate consequence. However, adding a bit more detail around the ‘why’ of the change and expanding on the context would elevate this answer to a stronger level. Focus on providing just enough background for the interviewer to understand the situation fully.\",\"suggested_answer\":\"While working on a software project focused on implementing user authentication, I made a mistake when I changed some of the code to update the user login functionality without testing it thoroughly first, which caused another part of the application to stop working. I realized there was an issue when I tried to use the feature later, so I went back through the code and eventually found the problem and fixed it. From that experience, I learned that I should test my changes more carefully before moving on to another part of the project. Since then, I have tried to spend more time checking my work and making sure the application still works after I make changes.\"}"]}
{"_e":"metro:client_log","_t":1786110555628,"level":"log","data":["Fifth answer saved:","{\"answer_id\": 35, \"feedback\": \"This is a solid, honest response demonstrating self-awareness and learning. The candidate clearly explains what happened and the immediate consequence. However, adding a bit more detail around the ‘why’ of the change and expanding on the context would elevate this answer to a stronger level. Focus on providing just enough background for the interviewer to understand the situation fully.\", \"improvements\": [\"**Situation (15/25):** The description is adequate, but could benefit from slightly more context. Adding one or two sentences about *why* they were changing the code would strengthen this. For example: 'While working on a software project focused on implementing user authentication...' This provides a better understanding of the situation.\", \"**Task (10/25):** The candidate states their responsibility – ‘changing some of the code’ – but doesn't explicitly state *what* they were trying to achieve with that change. Adding a brief explanation of the goal would improve clarity. For example: '…I was changing the code to update the user login functionality.'\"], \"scores\": {\"action\": 12, \"result\": 8, \"situation\": 15, \"task\": 10}, \"strengths\": [\"The candidate clearly identifies the core issue: changing code without thorough testing.\", \"They articulate a direct consequence of their action – another part of the application stopped working.\", \"The narrative flows logically from mistake to resolution.\"], \"suggested_answer\": \"While working on a software project focused on implementing user authentication, I made a mistake when I changed some of the code to update the user login functionality without testing it thoroughly first, which caused another part of the application to stop working. I realized there was an issue when I tried to use the feature later, so I went back through the code and eventually found the problem and fixed it. From that experience, I learned that I should test my changes more carefully before moving on to another part of the project. Since then, I have tried to spend more time checking my work and making sure the application still works after I make changes.\", \"total_score\": 45}"]}
